    "title": "No. 11 Bethel takes down second-ranked Grace - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Marini ,\n1 hours ago\nMISHAWAKA, Ind. (WANE) – Several former Highlight Zone standouts squared off Wednesday night in Mishawaka, with 11th-ranked Bethel topping no. 2 Grace 85-73 in a key Crossroads League men’s basketball game.\nWest Noble grad Austin Cripe led Bethel with 18 points, while Dwenger grad Beau Jacquay added 14 points and 8 rebounds. Norwell grad Luke McBride added 11 points for the Pilots.\nTyler Raasch led Grace with 16 points and 10 rebounds, while Blackhawk Christian grad Gage Sefton had 15 points. Warsaw grad Luke Bricker scored 10 points off the bench for the Lancers, while Manchester grad Gavin Betten chipped in with 8 points.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "(WANE) – Several former Highlight Zone standouts squared off Wednesday night in Mishawaka, with 11th-ranked Bethel topping no. 2 Grace 85-73 in a key Crossroads League men’s basketball game. West Noble grad Austin Cripe led Bethel with 18 points, while Dwenger grad Beau Jacquay added 14 points and 8 rebounds. Norwell grad Luke McBride added 11 points for the Pilots. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
